{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 04 - Retail Demand Forecasting & Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "## Objectives\n",
    "1. **Feature Invariance**: Verify autoregressive lag and rolling features avoid target leakage.\n",
    "2. **Chronological Splitting**: Split data into train and a 28-day out-of-sample test window with a common cutoff across all SKUs.\n",
    "3. **Seasonal Naive Baseline**: Evaluate 7-calendar-day seasonal persistence ($\hat{y}_{p,t} = y_{p, t-7}$).\n",
    "4. **Random Forest Regression**: Train Scikit-Learn `RandomForestRegressor` and enforce non-negative predictions.\n",
    "5. **Forecast Metrics**: Compare models using MAE, RMSE, and WAPE across identical evaluation observations.\n",
    "6. **Inspection**: Visualize actuals vs. model forecasts for representative product SKUs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add src to Python path\n",
    "sys.path.append(str(Path(\"..\").resolve() / \"src\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "from retail_forecasting.features.build_features import build_feature_pipeline\n",
    "from retail_forecasting.forecasting.baseline import SeasonalNaiveForecaster\n",
    "from retail_forecasting.forecasting.evaluate import compute_metrics, compute_per_product_metrics\n",
    "from retail_forecasting.forecasting.predict import generate_forecasts\n",
    "from retail_forecasting.forecasting.train import run_rolling_evaluation, temporal_train_test_split\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.style.use(\"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\" if \"seaborn-v0_8-whitegrid\" in plt.style.available else \"default\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load Processed Daily Demand & Generate Features\n",
    "\n",
    "We load `data/processed/daily_product_demand.parquet` and generate lag, rolling, and calendar features."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "demand_path = Path(\"../data/processed/daily_product_demand.parquet\")\n",
    "df_demand = pd.read_parquet(demand_path)\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(df_demand):,} records across {df_demand['product_id'].nunique():,} products.\")\n",
    "\n",
    "df_features = build_feature_pipeline(df_demand)\n",
    "print(f\"Feature matrix constructed: {df_features.shape[0]:,} rows, {df_features.shape[1]} columns.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Model-eligible observations (with 28-day history): {df_features['is_model_eligible'].sum():,}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Execute 28-Day Chronological Rolling Evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "Run rolling one-day-ahead evaluation comparing Seasonal Naive against Random Forest Regressor on identical product-date observations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "eval_results = run_rolling_evaluation(\n",
    "    feature_df=df_features,\n",
    "    test_days=28,\n",
    "    model_params={\"n_estimators\": 100, \"max_depth\": 10, \"random_state\": 42, \"n_jobs\": -1},\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "split_info = eval_results[\"split_report\"]\n",
    "print(\"--- Chronological Split Summary ---\")\n",
    "print(f\"Train Span: {split_info['min_date']} to {split_info['cutoff_date']} ({split_info['train_rows']:,} rows)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Test Span:  {split_info['test_start_date']} to {split_info['test_end_date']} ({split_info['test_rows']:,} rows)\")\n",
    "print(f\"Evaluation sample size: {eval_results['metrics']['evaluation_sample_size']:,} observations\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Compare Forecast Accuracy Metrics\n",
    "\n",
    "Evaluate Mean Absolute Error (MAE), Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE), and Weighted Absolute Percentage Error (WAPE)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "metrics = eval_results[\"metrics\"]\n",
    "comparison_df = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"Metric\": [\"Sample Size\", \"MAE (Units)\", \"RMSE (Units)\", \"WAPE (%)\"],\n",
    "    \"Seasonal Naive\": [\n",
    "        metrics[\"evaluation_sample_size\"],\n",
    "        metrics[\"seasonal_naive\"][\"mae\"],\n",
    "        metrics[\"seasonal_naive\"][\"rmse\"],\n",
    "        f\"{metrics['seasonal_naive']['wape']:.2f}%\"\n",
    "    ],\n",
    "    \"Random Forest\": [\n",
    "        metrics[\"evaluation_sample_size\"],\n",
    "        metrics[\"random_forest\"][\"mae\"],\n",
    "        metrics[\"random_forest\"][\"rmse\"],\n",
    "        f\"{metrics['random_forest']['wape']:.2f}%\"\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "})\n",
    "comparison_df"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Feature Importance Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "Inspect the relative predictive importance of lag, rolling, and calendar features in the Random Forest model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rf_model = eval_results[\"model\"]\n",
    "feature_names = eval_results[\"feature_cols\"]\n",
    "importances = pd.Series(rf_model.feature_importances_, index=feature_names).sort_values(ascending=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
    "importances.plot.barh(ax=ax, color=\"#2563EB\", edgecolor=\"none\", alpha=0.85)\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Random Forest Feature Importances\", fontweight=\"bold\", fontsize=13)\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Gini Importance\")\n",
    "fig.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Visual Inspection of Forecasts for Representative SKUs\n",
    "\n",
    "Plot actual test-period daily demand against Seasonal Naive and Random Forest predictions."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "eval_table = eval_results[\"evaluation_table\"]\n",
    "# Select a top-selling SKU with consistent sales\n",
    "top_skus = eval_table.groupby(\"product_id\")[\"actual_demand\"].sum().nlargest(3).index.tolist()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(len(top_skus), 1, figsize=(14, 4 * len(top_skus)), sharex=True)\n",
    "if len(top_skus) == 1:\n",
    "    axes = [axes]\n",
    "\n",
    "for ax, pid in zip(axes, top_skus):\n",
    "    sku_df = eval_table[eval_table[\"product_id\"] == pid].sort_values(\"date\")\n",
    "    ax.plot(sku_df[\"date\"], sku_df[\"actual_demand\"], label=\"Actual Demand\", color=\"#0F172A\", marker=\"o\", linewidth=1.5)\n",
    "    ax.plot(sku_df[\"date\"], sku_df[\"seasonal_naive_pred\"], label=\"Seasonal Naive (t-7)\", color=\"#F59E0B\", linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.7)\n",
    "    ax.plot(sku_df[\"date\"], sku_df[\"random_forest_pred\"], label=\"Random Forest\", color=\"#2563EB\", linewidth=2.0)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(f\"Product SKU: {pid} - Out-of-Sample Rolling Forecast\", fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"Daily Units Sold\")\n",
    "    ax.legend(loc=\"upper right\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
 ],
